IMPORT prelude

-- Bills of Sale Act 1886 (Singapore) -- what counts as a bill of sale (ss 2, 3), when a bill is void for want of attestation,
-- registration, a true consideration, the statutory form or a $100 minimum (ss 4, 6, 10), the schedule of chattels (s 5), rent and
-- property tax (s 7), when and how the lender may seize and sell (ss 8, 9), priority (s 11), transfers (s 12) and annual renewal
-- (s 13).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition ("incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"), informal consolidation,
-- version in force from 1/4/2022, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/BSA1886.txt. The latest amendment annotated in the
-- body is Act 25 of 2021 wef 01/04/2022 (s 8(1)(e), enforcement orders). The arrangement of sections at the top of the deposit is
-- one number out of step with the body (it lists "2. Short title"); the body's numbering is followed here.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0035 (subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl): Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a
-- sharper question yet. SCOPED to what a borrower who gives a bill of sale over his goods, or a lender who takes one, actually meets.
-- Not encoded: the trade-machinery and fixtures definitions beyond their effect in s 5(3), the "possession, order or disposition"
-- rule in bankruptcy (s 4(3), (4)), defeasances not in the body of the bill (s 10(4)), the register's form and entries (ss 14, 15),
-- rectification and satisfaction (ss 15, 16), search and copy fees (s 17), declarations, registrars, fees and rules (ss 18 to 21),
-- and the contents of the Schedules beyond the fact that the First Schedule form must be used. No fee rules or registry practice
-- were retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Bills of Sale Act 1886 -- bills of sale`

§§ `2, 3 -- what is a bill of sale`

-- s 3(1): "bill of sale" includes "assignments, transfers, declarations of trust without transfer ... and other assurances of
-- personal chattels, and also powers of attorney, authorities, or licences to take possession of personal chattels as security for
-- any debt", and "agreements for the hire of personal chattels entered into for the purpose of securing the repayment to the lessor
-- of such chattels of money advanced by him to the hirer" (the hirer is deemed the grantor). It "does not include" (a) assignments
-- for the benefit of creditors; (b) antenuptial marriage settlements; (c) transfers of any ship or share in one; (d) "transfers of
-- goods in the ordinary course of business of any trade or calling"; (e) bills of sale of goods in foreign parts or at sea;
-- (f) bills of lading and similar documents of title.
-- "personal chattels" does not include "shares or interests in the stocks ... or in the capital or property of incorporated or
-- joint-stock companies nor choses in action".
-- s 2(1): the Act does not, except as expressly mentioned, apply to "mortgages or debentures issued by any incorporated company and
-- secured upon the stock or goods". s 2(2): not to a bill executed on or after 1 May 2009 to the extent an interest in it is capable
-- of registration under the International Interests in Aircraft Equipment Act 2009.
-- (That an assignment of company shares is outside the Act is an inference from the definition of "personal chattels".)
DECLARE Instrument IS ONE OF
    `a written assignment of household furniture as security for a loan`
    `a hire agreement securing money the lessor advanced to the hirer`
    `a licence to take possession of goods as security for a debt`
    `an assignment for the benefit of the assignor's creditors`
    `an antenuptial marriage settlement`
    `a transfer of a ship`
    `a sale of goods in the ordinary course of a trade`
    `a debenture of an incorporated company secured on its goods`
    `an assignment of shares in a company`

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument, `the interest is registrable as an international interest in aircraft equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act applies to the instrument` IF
        (NOT `the interest is registrable as an international interest in aircraft equipment`)
    AND CONSIDER `the instrument`
        WHEN `a written assignment of household furniture as security for a loan` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a hire agreement securing money the lessor advanced to the hirer` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a licence to take possession of goods as security for a debt` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `10(2) -- who may attest`

-- s 10(2): execution "shall be attested -- (a) by an advocate and solicitor of the Supreme Court NOT being the advocate and solicitor
-- of the grantee; (b) by a Magistrate or by the Registrar or the Deputy Registrar of the Supreme Court; (c) by a commissioner for
-- oaths; or (d) by the registrar or deputy registrar" of bills of sale, "who shall personally explain to the grantor the effect
-- thereof, and the attestation shall state that before the execution ... the effect thereof was so explained".
DECLARE Attestor IS ONE OF
    `an advocate and solicitor not acting for the grantee`
    `the grantee's own advocate and solicitor`
    `a Magistrate`
    `a commissioner for oaths`
    `the registrar of bills of sale`
    `a friend of the grantor`

GIVEN `the attestor` IS AN Attestor, `the attestation states the effect was explained to the grantor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the bill is duly attested` IF
        `the attestation states the effect was explained to the grantor`
    AND CONSIDER `the attestor`
        WHEN `the grantee's own advocate and solicitor` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a friend of the grantor` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `4(1), 6, 10(3) -- when a bill given as security for money is void`

-- s 4(1): every bill of sale "shall be duly attested and shall be registered under this Act within 3 clear days after the execution
-- thereof, and shall truly set out the consideration for which it was given, otherwise ... (a) in the case of a bill of sale made or
-- given by way of security for the payment of money by the grantor thereof, such bill of sale shall be void in respect of the
-- personal chattels comprised therein".
-- s 6: a security bill "shall be void ... (a) if the amount the payment of which is thereby secured is less than $100; (b) if it is
-- not made in the form set out in the First Schedule; (c) if it is made or given wholly or in part in consideration of a
-- pre-existing debt".
-- Days are counted as day numbers. "Within 3 clear days after the execution" is read as: registration no later than the third day
-- after the day of execution. That reading is an INFERENCE; the text does not say how a Sunday or public holiday counts.
DECLARE `Security bill` HAS
    `duly attested` IS A BOOLEAN
    `day executed` IS A NUMBER
    `day registered` IS A NUMBER
    `consideration truly set out` IS A BOOLEAN
    `amount secured` IS A NUMBER
    `in the First Schedule form` IS A BOOLEAN
    `given for a pre-existing debt` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `executed on` IS A NUMBER, `filed on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `filed within 3 clear days` IF
    `filed on` AT LEAST `executed on` AND `filed on` MINUS `executed on` AT MOST 3

GIVEN `the bill` IS A `Security bill`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the security bill is void` IF
        (NOT `the bill`'s `duly attested`)
    OR  (NOT `filed within 3 clear days` (`the bill`'s `day executed`) (`the bill`'s `day registered`))
    OR  (NOT `the bill`'s `consideration truly set out`)
    OR  `the bill`'s `amount secured` LESS THAN 100
    OR  (NOT `the bill`'s `in the First Schedule form`)
    OR  `the bill`'s `given for a pre-existing debt`

§§ `4(1)(b), 4(2) -- an absolute bill that was not attested or registered`

-- s 4(1)(b): any OTHER (non-security) bill that fails s 4(1) is "deemed fraudulent and void" only "as against all trustees or
-- assignees of the estate of the person whose chattels ... are comprised in such bill of sale under the law of bankruptcy or
-- liquidation or under any assignment for the benefit of the creditors of such person, and also as against all sheriff's officers
-- and other persons seizing any chattels ... in the execution of any process of any court ... and also as against every person on
-- whose behalf such process shall have been issued", and only as to chattels which then, "and after the expiration of such 3 days are
-- in the possession or apparent possession" of the maker.
-- s 4(2): chattels are in apparent possession "so long as they remain ... upon any house, warehouse, shop ... or other premises
-- occupied by him, or are used and enjoyed by him in any place whatsoever, notwithstanding that formal possession ... may have been
-- taken".
DECLARE Challenger IS ONE OF
    `the grantor himself`
    `the grantor's trustee in bankruptcy`
    `a sheriff's officer seizing under court process`
    `the creditor who obtained the process`
    `a neighbour with no claim on the grantor`

GIVEN `on premises the grantor occupies` IS A BOOLEAN, `used and enjoyed by the grantor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the chattels are in the grantor's apparent possession` IF
    `on premises the grantor occupies` OR `used and enjoyed by the grantor`

GIVEN `complied with s 4(1)` IS A BOOLEAN, `the challenger` IS A Challenger, `in apparent possession after the 3 days` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the absolute bill is void against the challenger` IF
        (NOT `complied with s 4(1)`)
    AND `in apparent possession after the 3 days`
    AND CONSIDER `the challenger`
        WHEN `the grantor himself` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a neighbour with no claim on the grantor` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `5 -- the schedule of chattels`

-- s 5(1): the bill "shall have effect only in respect of the personal chattels specifically described in that schedule and shall be
-- void in respect of any personal chattels not so specifically described". (2): void as to scheduled chattels "of which the grantor
-- was not the true owner at the time of the execution". (3): but not void as to (a) growing crops separately assigned "actually
-- growing at the time when the bill of sale was executed", or (b) fixtures, plant or trade machinery brought upon the premises "in
-- substitution for any of the like fixtures, plant or trade machinery specifically described in the schedule".
GIVEN `specifically described in the schedule` IS A BOOLEAN, `the grantor owned it at execution` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a crop growing at execution and separately assigned` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `fixtures, plant or trade machinery substituted for scheduled items` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the bill has effect over the chattel` IF
        (`specifically described in the schedule` AND `the grantor owned it at execution`)
    OR  `a crop growing at execution and separately assigned`
    OR  `fixtures, plant or trade machinery substituted for scheduled items`

§§ `7 -- rent and property tax`

-- s 7: a security bill "shall be no protection against a distress for the recovery of rent or property tax".
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a security bill protects the chattels against a distress for rent or property tax` IF FALSE

§§ `8(1) -- the only causes for seizure`

-- s 8(1): chattels in a security bill "shall not be liable to be seized or taken possession of by the grantee for any other than the
-- following causes: (a) if the grantor makes default in payment ... at the time therein provided for payment or in the performance of
-- any covenant ... necessary for maintaining the security; (b) if the grantor becomes a bankrupt or suffers the chattels ... to be
-- distrained for rent, property tax or otherwise; (c) if the grantor fraudulently either removes or suffers to be removed from the
-- premises the chattels ...; (d) if the grantor does not without reasonable excuse upon demand in writing by the grantee produce to
-- him his last receipts for rent and property tax; (e) if an enforcement order has been executed against the goods of the grantor".
DECLARE Cause IS ONE OF
    `default in paying an instalment when due`
    `the grantor became a bankrupt`
    `the chattels were distrained for rent`
    `the grantor fraudulently removed the chattels from the premises`
    `no rent and property tax receipts produced on written demand without reasonable excuse`
    `an enforcement order executed against the grantor's goods`
    `the grantee fears the goods are losing value`
    `the grantee wants the money back early`

GIVEN `the cause` IS A Cause
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the grantee may seize for the cause` IF
    CONSIDER `the cause`
    WHEN `the grantee fears the goods are losing value` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the grantee wants the money back early` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `8(2), 8(3) -- five days on the premises, and the grantor's application`

-- s 8(2): seized chattels "shall remain on the premises ... and shall not be removed or sold until after the expiration of 5 clear
-- days from the day on which they were so seized". s 8(3): the grantor "may within 5 days from the seizure ... apply to the General
-- Division of the High Court", which, "if satisfied that by payment of money or otherwise the said cause of seizure no longer
-- exists, may restrain the grantee from removing or selling the chattels".
-- INFERENCE: "5 clear days from the day" excludes the day of seizure, so the first day removal or sale is allowed is the sixth day
-- after it. "Within 5 days from the seizure" is read as up to and including the fifth day after it.
GIVEN `seized on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first day the chattels may be removed or sold` MEANS `seized on` PLUS 6

GIVEN `seized on` IS A NUMBER, `on day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the chattels may be removed or sold` IF
    `on day` AT LEAST `the first day the chattels may be removed or sold` `seized on`

GIVEN `seized on` IS A NUMBER, `applied on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the grantor's application to the High Court is in time` IF
    `applied on` AT LEAST `seized on` AND `applied on` MINUS `seized on` AT MOST 5

§§ `9 -- sale by public auction, and one year's interest`

-- s 9(1): "No sale by the grantee of any chattels so seized ... shall be made otherwise than by public auction, conducted by some
-- person duly licensed under any statutory provision for the licensing of auctioneers." (2): a contravening sale "shall be absolutely
-- void, and any person aiding or abetting such sale shall be liable to a fine not exceeding $200". (3): "Not more than one year's
-- arrears of interest shall be recoverable under any bill of sale."
GIVEN `by public auction` IS A BOOLEAN, `by a licensed auctioneer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sale is valid` IF `by public auction` AND `by a licensed auctioneer`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for aiding or abetting a void sale` MEANS 200

GIVEN `first amount` IS A NUMBER, `second amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS IF `first amount` AT MOST `second amount` THEN `first amount` ELSE `second amount`

GIVEN `interest in arrears` IS A NUMBER, `interest for one year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the arrears of interest recoverable` MEANS `the lesser of` `interest in arrears` `interest for one year`

§§ `11 -- priority`

-- s 11: where two or more bills comprise any of the same chattels "they shall have priority in the order of the date of their
-- registration". The date of execution plays no part. (Two registrations on the same date are not dealt with; not encoded.)
GIVEN `first bill executed on` IS A NUMBER, `first bill registered on` IS A NUMBER,
      `second bill executed on` IS A NUMBER, `second bill registered on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first bill has priority` IF
    `first bill registered on` LESS THAN `second bill registered on`

§§ `12 -- transfers of a registered bill`

-- s 12: a transfer "need not be attested", but the transferee "shall within 3 clear days after the execution of the transfer ... file
-- with the registrar a statutory declaration in the form set out in the Second Schedule ... and shall also produce at the same time to
-- the registrar the said transfer ..., otherwise the said transfer or assignment shall be void". (3 clear days read as in s 4.)
GIVEN `transfer executed on` IS A NUMBER, `declaration filed on` IS A NUMBER, `transfer produced to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transfer is valid` IF
    `filed within 3 clear days` `transfer executed on` `declaration filed on` AND `transfer produced to the registrar`

§§ `13 -- renewal every 12 months`

-- s 13(1): registration "shall be renewed once at least every 12 calendar months, and if a period of 12 calendar months elapses from
-- the registration or renewed registration ... without a renewal ... the registration shall become void". Counted here in complete
-- calendar months; whether a renewal on the anniversary itself is in time is not settled by the text (INFERENCE: it is taken as late).
GIVEN `complete months since the last registration or renewal` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the registration has become void` IF
    `complete months since the last registration or renewal` AT LEAST 12
